                <pb facs="1158" n="1048" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg1048"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.79611 Pangborn-Herndon Flight/36:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Forbes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-08-10T17:00:00+09:00">August 10, 1931—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 10—9:50 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>117. Embassy’s telegram 80, June 11, noon. Herndon and Pang-born landed in Japan,
                    August 7th, without permit after flying over several fortified zones taking
                    moving pictures on the way. They have spent a very bad week end with the police
                    but have not been actually arrested. The Embassy is using its good offices to
                    mitigate official displeasure. Result uncertain as yet.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Forbes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
